**FoodcoopBCN is the first cooperative, participatory and non-profit supermarket in Barcelona.** It belongs to its members, and its most important decisions are taken by all of them in the general assembly.

On September 21, 2026, FoodcoopBCN held one of the most important assemblies in its history: a vote to **decide the future of the cooperative**. The Consell Rector, the cooperative's governing board, was clear that a decision of this size needed as many voices as possible. So they ran a **hybrid general assembly with Vocdoni**: members in the room voted on paper, and members at home followed the assembly by livestream and voted online.

The result: **115 votes, 12.6% of the membership**, and a decision the whole cooperative could stand behind.

## Key facts

- **Organization:** FoodcoopBCN, cooperative supermarket in Barcelona
- **Vote:** general assembly on the future of the cooperative
- **Date:** September 21, 2026
- **Format:** hybrid, with paper ballots in the room and online voting from home
- **Votes cast:** 115 (85 in person and 30 online), 12.6% of a census of 916 members
- **Online voting:** anonymous vote, encrypted until the close, with verifiable results
- **Run by:** the cooperative itself in the [Vocdoni App](https://app.vocdoni.io), from the member list to assembly day

## What FoodcoopBCN is

FoodcoopBCN started in 2018 as an association to bring the participatory supermarket model to Barcelona, inspired by Park Slope Food Coop in New York. Its shop on Passatge d'Aragó opened in 2022.

The model is simple: **the members own the supermarket**. Consumer members contribute a few hours a month to running the shop, and every member has a voice and a vote in the assembly, where the big decisions are made.

## The challenge: a decision that needed legitimacy

When the question on the table is the future of the cooperative itself, the result has to be beyond doubt. That means two things: **a process members can trust**, and **enough participation for the result to represent the membership**.

An assembly held only in person makes the second part hard. Members have jobs, children, care duties and lives that don't always fit an evening in a meeting room. Some live in other parts of the city or outside it. In a cooperative with hundreds of members, an in-person-only assembly leaves out most of them by default.

The Consell Rector wanted every member to be able to take part, wherever they were. They needed:

- **One assembly, two ways to vote**, so members in the room and at home took part in the same decision
- **Reliable identification**, so only members voted and each of them voted once
- **An anonymous vote**, so no one could see how any member voted
- **Results that could be checked**, available as soon as voting closed
- **A process the cooperative could run on its own**, without hiring a technical team

## How the hybrid assembly worked

**In the room:** members attending the assembly at the cooperative voted on paper.

**At home:** members who could not attend followed the assembly by livestream. When the time came to vote, they opened the voting link, identified themselves as members and cast their vote from their phone or computer. No app to download and no account to create.

**The online vote:** each online ballot was anonymous, because each member's identification and their vote were kept separate and could not be linked. Ballots also stayed encrypted until the vote closed, so no partial results could influence anyone still deciding. When voting closed, the online votes were tallied automatically and added to the paper count.

### Run by the cooperative, from start to finish

FoodcoopBCN did not need an IT department or an external provider to run the assembly. The cooperative's own team used the [Vocdoni App](https://app.vocdoni.io) for every step:

1. **Managing the census.** They uploaded and maintained the list of members entitled to vote.
2. **Creating the vote.** They configured the question and the options for the assembly.
3. **Running assembly day.** They opened and closed the online vote in step with the assembly and got the results the moment it closed.

For hybrid assemblies, the Vocdoni App also lets administrators [update the census while a vote is live](/blog/vocdoni-app-2-3-adds-hybrid-voting-support-weighted-voting-vote-delegation-and-more), for example to remove online access for a member who has already voted on paper.

